```python
import numpy as np
from scipy.special import logsumexp

def log_softmax(z, axis=-1):
    z = np.asarray(z, dtype=float)
    return z - logsumexp(z, axis=axis, keepdims=True)

def softmax(z, axis=-1):
    return np.exp(log_softmax(z, axis))

softmax([1000, 1001, 1002])   # [0.0900, 0.2447, 0.6652], no nan
```

Note `keepdims=True`: it keeps the reduced axis as size 1 so the subtraction broadcasts row by row when `z` has shape (batch, K). Forgetting it is the most common shape bug in hand-written softmax.
